# lab/ is the instrument. Every reading a run takes — its vault, its
# snapshots, its report, its logs and its transcripts — lands under `runs/`,
# which is ignored whole. Nothing a run produces is committed: re-run to see
# it again, and the plan document records what it showed.
#
# A run's directory is also the only thing mounted into the container beside
# what the build writes, so keeping readings out of here is what lets those be
# mounted read-only.
__pycache__/
lint*.md
coherence*.md
# the build output, and only that: without the leading slash this also matches
# `harness/src/bin/`, where the binaries' own sources live
/bin/
